jichi
  jichi Desktop is a client for jichi, an AI agent written by
  Alexander-Lars Dallmann; copyright (c) 2026 Justus-Liebig-Universität
  Gießen, licensed under Apache-2.0
  (https://github.com/alexanderlarsdallmann/jichi).
  This repository contains no jichi source code. jichi runs as a separate
  program that the application starts (`jichi --acp`), and its
  documentation is read from jichi's own source tree at run time.
  The demo fixture under screenshots/ quotes a few jichi documentation pages
  and the output of `jichi init`; those quotes remain under jichi's licence.

JLU Design System (@ki4jlu/design-system)
  Colours and type come from the JLU Design System, referenced as a build
  dependency and not included in this repository. Its package declares no
  open-source licence ("UNLICENSED"). Redistributing built application
  bundles needs the permission of its authors.

DejaVu fonts (src-tauri/fonts/)
  Embedded for PDF export. Bitstream Vera / DejaVu licence, see
  src-tauri/fonts/DejaVu-LICENSE.txt.

